WEBVTT

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:19.500
Rain, huh?

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:24.900
I could go yell in the rain.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.360
I guess I won't need an umbrella.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:40.940
I don't know how I feel about yelling, though.

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:48.590
What is Tsuchida-sensei doing?

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:55.620
Perhaps he tried to invoke a sense of drama by yelling but was too embarrassed to actually do it.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:58.420
I don't know if I can greet him.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:03.010
What am I doing?

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:10.380
Then the dog said, "Won't you give me one of those dumplings?"

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.730
Momotaro was pleased to have a strong companion.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.270
Tsuchida, this is boring!

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:17.390
We already know the story of Momotaro.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.050
Don't you have anything more interesting?

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:21.610
I know, right?

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:23.520
Really?

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:26.620
I mean, things are just starting to get interesting.

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:29.740
Uh, where were we?

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:33.390
What's wrong, Tsuchida-kun? Cheer up.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.800
A gloomy teacher isn't good for the children.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:38.360
Right, of course.

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:40.220
Are you feeling unwell?

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:42.050
No, that's not...

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:45.350
Oh, hello.

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:49.850
"A Hanamaru Wife"

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.980
Yes, I've got a bit of a cold.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:57.860
Yes, I think I'll get better if I take the day off.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.430
Sorry for the inconvenience.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:02.250
Yes.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:05.830
I took the day off.

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:10.120
Work, huh?

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:16.260
Who is that?

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.240
Could it be Yamamoto-sensei?

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.290
No, I guess not.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:25.080
She doesn't know I live in this apartment, anyway.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:31.810
Hello, Tsuchi!

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:35.240
That's great, but what are you doing here?

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:39.170
I came to take care of you and help you get better sooner.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:40.210
Take care of me?

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:41.550
Excuse me!

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:42.450
Hey!

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:47.300
This is the first time I've been inside your home.

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:52.420
Listen, I don't want to give you my cold, so why don't you...

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:55.680
Don't worry about it. Just get some rest.

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:58.270
I'll take care of you today.

00:02:58.330 --> 00:02:59.530
But...

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:02.470
You can think of me as your bride today.

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:05.170
We'll be getting married eventually anyway.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:09.890
Um, what is it called? Reversal?

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.090
Rehearsal?

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:15.020
Yeah, that! Today you can leave everything to me.

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:20.950
Here, my mommy said tangerines are good for colds.

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:22.000
Really?

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:28.400
I'll start by tidying up the kitchen.

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:31.450
Tidy up? Are you going to be okay?

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.610
I'll be fine.

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:39.230
Look at you. You've allowed all these dishes to pile up.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.540
Let's see, where's the soap?

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:47.990
This stuff is dangerous, so don't touch it.

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:51.760
Sorry. I'll go clean.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.010
There shouldn't be anything dangerous about that.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:04.970
I'm fine, I'm fine. I don't need any help.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:05.870
Sure, sure.

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:10.250
How did you even manage to do this?

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.600
Ow, it hurts!

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:12.510
Oh, sorry.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:18.670
I'm not going to have any time to relax.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.210
Look at all of these.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:24.880
Don't bring these out!

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:27.880
Don't worry, I don't mind your dirty magazines.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:29.770
Either way, you still can't look at them!

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:32.820
I want to know what you're into.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.100
You really are a breast man, huh?

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:38.220
So? I can like what I want!

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:39.850
Oh, men.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:42.580
What did you say?

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:46.770
There's nothing in here.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.000
I don't cook for myself much.

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:50.380
What am I going to do?

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:53.280
Why don't I make you some ramen?

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:55.400
You're going to cook for me?

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:56.700
But your cold...

00:04:57.470 --> 00:04:58.980
I can handle this much.

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:12.840
Oh, Sakura-senpai? It's me.

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:15.220
Tsuchi, how's your cold?

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:19.010
Taking care of Anzu seems to have driven it away.

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:25.630
Sorry about that. She said she'd take care of you, but did she cause trouble instead?

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:27.700
Oh, it's no big deal.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:29.850
What's Anzu up to right now?

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:32.480
She fell asleep.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:36.110
She could stay here tonight, if that's alright.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:44.290
That'd be great. Could you take her to breakfast at a diner tomorrow?

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:46.110
I'll pay you back later.

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:47.900
Sure, but why?

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:51.300
I'm trying to finish a ton of work.

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:55.220
There's so much to do for the magazine's extra issue.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:58.810
Extra issue? Oh, your job as a writer?

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:00.250
Got it.

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:01.370
Thanks again.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:05.510
Tsuchi.

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:07.510
I love you.

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:14.750
Hii-chan, Koume-chan!

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:15.660
What?

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:21.810
I spent the night with Tsuchi yesterday.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.410
Spent the night together?

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:26.990
That's great. A sleepover at Tsuchida-sensei's house.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:28.840
You're a woman now, Anzu-chan.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:31.790
We drank our morning coffee together.

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:33.080
I didn't have coffee, though...

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:33.690
Anzu-san!

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:36.740
I can't believe how immoral you are!

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:44.350
You went to visit Tsuchida-sensei and fell asleep?

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:45.360
Yeah.

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:49.080
Why did you have to make it sound so suggestive?

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:53.070
Has Tsuchida-sensei gotten over his cold?

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:54.260
Yeah.

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:56.460
He came to the kindergarten today.

00:06:56.820 --> 00:07:00.620
His cold is better, but he still seems down.

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:06.740
Could his mind still be on Yamamoto-sensei?

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:08.070
Probably.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:14.660
His confession to Yamamoto-sensei didn't go over well?

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:17.000
What do you want to do about it, Anzu?

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.600
I want Tsuchi to be happy again.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:20.760
But...

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:22.130
But...?

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:27.100
If he cheers up again, he might fall in love with Yamamoto-sensei again.

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:32.520
I see. You don't want Tsuchi to be unhappy...

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:37.040
...but you don't want him to cheer up and confess to Yamamoto-sensei again.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:39.050
That's a tough one.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:39.940
Isn't it?

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:48.090
Thinking about it won't do you any good. Why don't you just hope he cheers up?

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:48.950
But...

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:53.880
Don't worry. As long as you keep supporting him, he'll notice how you feel eventually.

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:55.000
Really?

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:57.590
Really. I promise.

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:01.800
Nothing is stronger than the power of love.

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:06.180
"The power of love?" You mentioned that before, didn't you?

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:08.820
Yup, that's the magic of love.

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:11.650
I think it'll be especially effective on Tsuchi.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:21.870
I'm back! Today I'll be doing your laundry.

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:24.660
My cold is all better, though.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:27.160
Don't worry about that.

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:28.930
I'm not sure I...

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:34.840
My mommy said a woman who travels to her husband's house every day is called a "commuting wife."

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:38.270
What are you teaching her now, senpai?

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:41.780
Look at you. You've allowed all this laundry to pile up.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.550
I don't have a laundry machine.

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:46.520
You use a coin-op laundromat, don't you?

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:50.050
Don't worry, I've used one before.

00:08:50.110 --> 00:08:51.400
Hey, Anzu.

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:55.540
Wait, I'll go with you.

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:18.120
Anzu? What are you...

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:20.850
Good morning, Tsuchi. Did you sleep well?

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:21.930
How'd you get in here?

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:23.380
Tada!

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:25.820
The landlord let me borrow a key.

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:27.370
Oh, really?

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:38.120
It's still pretty early. I guess I'll take her home.

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:48.920
"A Hanamaru Story"

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:52.500
Thank you for bringing her home.

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:53.750
It's no trouble.

00:09:54.880 --> 00:09:56.860
Why don't you stay for some tea?

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:01.590
My husband has been staying cooped up in his studio in preparation for his show.

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:03.350
His show, huh?

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:07.770
By the way, is that the work you mentioned before?

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:11.500
Yeah, the 90's youth catalogue.

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:13.140
Kogyaru and pagers.

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:17.880
We're already reminiscing about what feels like just yesterday.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:22.940
It's an interesting project, but with the deadline only a week away...

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:27.280
...people have been getting sick and hurting themselves, and now we're short staffed.

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:29.040
What did you do?

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:33.790
I told them to leave it to me and took on their work, too.

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:37.210
It was more work than I thought it would be.

00:10:37.210 --> 00:10:39.290
I haven't slept properly in days.

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:41.890
You haven't changed a bit, senpai.

00:10:42.090 --> 00:10:44.870
I know! why don't you help me write, Tsuchi?

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:46.420
I'm sure you'd be able to write something about games.

00:10:46.550 --> 00:10:50.740
Me? I'm not really in the mood to...

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:51.930
Just do it.

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:57.390
Tsuchi, this is great.

00:10:57.390 --> 00:10:58.320
Really?

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:01.650
I'd have to fix it up a little, but I can definitely use this.

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:02.910
Really?

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:05.650
I hate to ask, but could you write a little more?

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:08.830
Sure. I've got the day off tomorrow anyway.

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:15.290
Saito-kun's cat? What are we going to do?

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:17.850
What did he still have left to do?

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:19.610
Karaoke and...

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:22.540
Tsuchi, would you be able to write about shonen manga?

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:24.540
Sure.

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:30.340
I can't believe I'm getting more work at this stage.

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:32.660
Let's see, karaoke...

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:36.190
You seem to enjoy your job, Sakura-senpai.

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:39.800
I guess so. Don't you enjoy your job, Tsuchi?

00:11:41.990 --> 00:11:46.450
I've always liked working with kids, so I enjoy it.

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:51.160
I've just started wondering what I'm working for.

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:54.420
Is that what you're depressed about?

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:58.170
It's not because your confession to Yamamoto-sensei didn't go over well?

00:11:58.460 --> 00:11:59.890
How did you know about that?

00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:02.100
Because Anzu told me, of course.

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:03.410
Oh, right.

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:10.390
I used to think I couldn't even confess my feelings to someone I liked.

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:17.640
The more I thought about it, the more I began to think I'd be better suited to a different job.

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:21.690
That got me wondering about the meaning of work.

00:12:22.530 --> 00:12:28.940
You worry too much. Have you only been working to impress Yamamoto-sensei?

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:33.760
That may have been part of it.

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:36.230
Do you think that was the wrong thing to do?

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:39.120
There's nothing wrong with that kind of motivation.

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:42.320
But don't you think work is bigger than that?

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:44.000
Bigger?

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:48.520
Something to live for or improve yourself.

00:12:49.150 --> 00:12:51.550
It's always fun to work with someone, too.

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:57.890
That's easy for you to say since you're living life to the fullest.

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:00.310
You think so?

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:06.190
In any case, cheer up. What are the girls going to do with a gloomy teacher?

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:15.300
So Anzu was coming to my apartment because she was worried about me, huh?

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:19.930
I can't keep making everyone worry.

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:22.600
I've got to settle this.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:24.760
I'll ask Yamamoto-sensei how she feels.

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:27.430
If she says no, at least I'll be able to move on.

00:13:28.060 --> 00:13:29.490
"Dear Anzu, I'm heading out for a bit. I'll be back this evening."

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:35.610
What a luxurious mansion.

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:41.580
I came all the way here, but is it alright for me to show up unannounced?

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:45.200
I've even got these flowers.

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:47.350
Will I seem like a weirdo?

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:51.910
Even if I do meet with Yamamoto-sensei, what am I supposed to say?

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:55.290
Am I just going to ask her what she thinks of me?

00:13:56.530 --> 00:13:57.820
I should just go home.

00:13:58.570 --> 00:14:00.940
Is that you, Tsuchida-san?

00:14:02.390 --> 00:14:04.470
You're Yamamoto-sensei's...

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:06.210
Her sister Mayumi.

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:08.590
Hello.

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:12.100
What are you doing here today. Are you here to see my sister?

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:15.470
Yamamoto-sensei lives near here?

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:17.390
What a coincidence.

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:19.040
Those flowers and his attitude.

00:14:20.220 --> 00:14:22.720
I knew Tsuchida-san had feelings for my sister.

00:14:23.140 --> 00:14:26.230
Tsuchida-san, my sister is at the kindergarten today.

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:28.230
The kindergarten? On a Sunday?

00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:30.690
She said she had something to take care of.

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:35.740
Is that so? Well, I've got something to do, so I'll see you later.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:42.080
He showed up at your apartment with flowers?

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:45.870
Tsuchida-san must be in love with my sister.

00:14:45.950 --> 00:14:49.720
She's so dense she hasn't noticed.

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:52.130
Your sister's dense, huh?

00:14:52.940 --> 00:14:57.300
By the way, Hanamaru-sensei, why did you invite me to a play?

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:03.350
I thought it might be useful for my next manuscript, so I thought it'd be good for you to see it.

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:05.050
Is that so?

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:12.170
I wish Yamamoto-san would realize she's dense, too.

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:24.000
Tsuchida-sensei...

00:15:24.330 --> 00:15:26.220
What are you doing here on a Sunday?

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:28.410
I just had some work to do.

00:15:29.310 --> 00:15:30.430
Is it paperwork?

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:36.560
"Dear Keita-kun's mother, something wonderful happened this past Friday."

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:39.430
Please don't embarrass me by reading this.

00:15:40.930 --> 00:15:42.940
Are those letters to the parents?

00:15:43.470 --> 00:15:47.960
Yes. I work slowly, so I can never get it all in the report book.

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:51.690
I try to write letters once in a while.

00:15:52.190 --> 00:15:54.820
How considerate. You're writing so many, too.

00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:56.410
That's amazing.

00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:57.780
It's nothing.

00:15:59.380 --> 00:16:02.070
What are you doing at the kindergarten today, Tsuchida-sensei?

00:16:03.030 --> 00:16:05.630
Me? I, uh...

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:10.660
Flowers! I found some cheap flowers, so I thought we could decorate the staff office with them.

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:12.330
How wonderful.

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:20.430
Seeing you write those letters made me realize you really like working at the kindergarten.

00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:22.500
Yes, I love my job.

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:30.090
You mentioned something before about being inspired by your own kindergarten teacher.

00:16:30.570 --> 00:16:37.180
Yes, I eventually realized I'm not particularly bright or talented...

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:45.350
...but I thought I might be able to become a teacher if I tried hard enough.

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:52.160
I don't have much experience yet, but I love being able to work with children every day.

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:55.340
Working with children makes me feel...

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:08.310
I'm sorry. I lose sight of my surroundings when I get caught up in my thoughts.

00:17:08.550 --> 00:17:10.260
Uh, Yamamoto-sensei...

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:11.500
Yes?

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:15.130
If a man were to say, uh...

00:17:15.670 --> 00:17:18.950
...he liked you and asked you on a date, what would you do?

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:26.450
I think I'd be very happy to hear someone say that.

00:17:27.390 --> 00:17:28.000
But...

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:29.250
But...?

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:32.990
I'm not sure I would be able to handle that.

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:37.800
My hands are full trying to becoming a full-fledged teacher.

00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:41.060
I'm not sure I would have the time and energy for a relationship.

00:17:46.260 --> 00:17:48.460
What's wrong, Tsuchida-sensei?

00:17:49.530 --> 00:17:55.080
It's nothing. I'm glad we got to talk today.

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:58.720
I just remembered I've got something to do, so I've got to get going.

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:10.570
Yamamoto-sensei is amazing.

00:18:11.410 --> 00:18:13.460
She's so passionate about her job.

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:17.270
She'd never be a match for a half-hearted guy like me.

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:20.610
Not a match, huh?

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:23.810
What do I have?

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:26.600
Welcome home, Tsuchi.

00:18:26.990 --> 00:18:28.590
You're here, huh?

00:18:29.070 --> 00:18:31.220
You're late, Tsuchi. It's already night.

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:32.720
Sorry.

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:35.310
I guess I can forgive you since you apologized.

00:18:35.570 --> 00:18:38.860
I made you a home cooked meal for dinner tonight.

00:18:39.150 --> 00:18:40.010
Home cooked?

00:18:42.290 --> 00:18:44.400
I don't know about your cooking...

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:47.290
Don't worry. It's delicious this time.

00:18:47.490 --> 00:18:49.610
I'll make some fried eggs. You just watch.

00:18:49.890 --> 00:18:50.750
Watch you?

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:55.750
I'm just a kid, so I need adult supervision when using the stove.

00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:57.410
Oh, right.

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:05.420
Let's eat.

00:19:09.470 --> 00:19:10.520
This is good.

00:19:10.610 --> 00:19:11.460
Really?

00:19:11.860 --> 00:19:13.320
Did you really make this?

00:19:13.700 --> 00:19:18.030
I made the pork and potatoes and spinach at home with my mommy.

00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:19.700
Really? How impressive.

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:23.690
I've been practicing cooking ever since I made you lunch.

00:19:24.090 --> 00:19:25.530
Did you do that for me?

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:29.290
Yeah, I just wanted to make you something delicious.

00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:33.060
What's wrong, Tsuchi?

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:35.030
Nothing.

00:19:35.790 --> 00:19:38.850
Anzu's smile almost made me feel something.

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:42.280
I'm stuffed.

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:45.910
Tsuchi, did you like my dinner?

00:19:46.020 --> 00:19:47.210
Yeah, it was delicious.

00:19:48.610 --> 00:19:51.230
Tell me a story, Tsuchi.

00:19:51.390 --> 00:19:53.400
You sound like such a child.

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:54.990
I am a child!

00:19:54.990 --> 00:19:56.000
Oh, right.

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:57.720
Let's see.

00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:01.870
Once upon a time, there was an old couple.

00:20:01.870 --> 00:20:04.880
Not one of those! I want an interesting story!

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:06.780
An interesting story, huh?

00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:11.810
Oh, I know.

00:20:12.530 --> 00:20:15.660
In the land of fairy tales, there lived a prince known as Prince Clumsy.

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:17.490
Prince Clumsy?

00:20:17.680 --> 00:20:21.840
Yup, he's a nice guy, but he can't do anything right.

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:23.690
He's really that clumsy?

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:27.600
Super clumsy. He could make it into the Guinness Book of World Records.

00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:30.070
This sounds like it could be an interesting story.

00:20:30.860 --> 00:20:34.430
Prince Clumsy was in love with Princess Dense from the neighboring kingdom.

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:35.800
Princess Dense?

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:38.180
Yup, this princess was quite a character, too.

00:20:38.860 --> 00:20:41.230
Tsuchida-san was at the kindergarten today, wasn't he?

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:42.790
Yes, he was.

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:44.910
What did you talk to him about?

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:49.880
What did we talk about? How working at the kindergarten is a worthwhile and fun job.

00:20:49.910 --> 00:20:50.850
Are you serious?

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:53.950
Tsuchida-sensei is a great listener. I went on and on.

00:20:54.250 --> 00:20:56.710
That's when the villainous panda-cat appeared.

00:20:56.970 --> 00:20:59.620
Panda-cat is a champion of justice.

00:21:00.010 --> 00:21:03.640
Exactly. It was a panda-cat impostor.

00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:09.480
But Prince Clumsy and Princess Dense didn't realize it and let the impostor into their castle.

00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:14.290
What do you think of Tsuchida-san, Nana-chan?

00:21:14.350 --> 00:21:16.850
He's a wonderful person.

00:21:16.850 --> 00:21:17.630
Really?

00:21:17.770 --> 00:21:23.320
Yes, he instantly became friends with the children at the kindergarten.

00:21:23.890 --> 00:21:27.300
The children even have a nickname for him. It's amazing.

00:21:27.420 --> 00:21:29.480
So that's what she meant.

00:21:29.570 --> 00:21:32.820
It sounds like Tsuchida-san might have a chance, though.

00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:36.410
That's when the real panda-cat showed up to save them.

00:21:36.660 --> 00:21:39.300
Hooray! Tsuchi, what happened next?

00:21:39.370 --> 00:21:45.520
But that's when the panda-cat impostor became a giant. He was bigger than the castle.

00:21:45.940 --> 00:21:47.640
Even panda-cat couldn't stand a chance.

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:49.380
And that's when Prince Clumsy...

00:21:50.390 --> 00:21:51.890
What do you think Prince Clumsy did?

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:53.350
Did he try to fight?

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:58.310
Nope, he ran to the basement under the castle.

00:23:30.440 --> 00:23:33.270
Anzu here! Next week is finally the last episode.

00:23:33.270 --> 00:23:36.340
I had so much fun during our time together.

00:23:36.430 --> 00:23:40.560
The last episode is about Christmas and another one of Tsuchi's confessions.

00:23:40.670 --> 00:23:42.190
Don't miss the last episode.

00:23:42.260 --> 00:23:43.500
"A Hanamaru Christmas"

00:23:42.390 --> 00:23:44.700
Take care, everyone. Bye-bye!

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:44.700
"Hanamaru Feelings"

00:23:44.700 --> 00:23:49.470
"See you next time!"
